more pungs (e.g., J1 pung and T9 pung or W4 pung) to have four pungs/kongs, giving All Pungs (6) + Dragon Pung x2 (4) = 10 points. That meets 8. Also, if I get a kong, maybe Three Kongs (32 points) but I already have one kong, so need two more kongs. Unlikely.  \n\nTherefore, preserving the possibility of All Pungs is valuable. Chi T7 would introduce a chow, breaking All Pungs. So I should Pass to keep hand flexible for pungs.  \n\nAlso, T7 discard might be safe for others? But my priority is to improve my own hand.  \n\nGiven the above, I think Pass is better to maintain higher scoring potential.  \n\nReason: Passing allows me to draw a tile and keep the option to pursue All Pungs (6 points) combined with Dragon Pung(s), which could easily reach the 8-point threshold. Chi T7 would commit me to a chow, reducing the chance for All Pungs and potentially lowering my score.  \n\nAnswer: Pass"}
